---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = "Your China Trip Survival Kit: Everything You Need Before You Go";
const description = "From apps and SIM cards to VPN and packing — here's your complete pre-travel checklist for China.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} lang="fr">
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-8 not-prose">
      <a href="/fr/life/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-700 transition no-underline group">
        <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 transition-transform group-hover:-translate-x-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"/>
        </svg>
        Back to Life
      </a>
    </nav>
    <header class="mb-12">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-3">🎒 Life in China</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4 leading-tight">
        Your China Trip Survival Kit<br class="hidden md:block" />: Everything You Need Before You Go
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-6">Five things to sort out before your trip — none are difficult, but each one matters.</p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-gray-500">
        <span>📅 Last updated: June 2026</span>
        <span>⏱️ 6 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

        <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-green-50 to-emerald-50 border-l-4 border-green-500 rounded-r-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-900 mb-4">🎯 Quick Answer</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-green-800 leading-relaxed">
        <strong>There are five things you need to sort out before your China trip: your phone, your internet connection, your VPN, a few basic Chinese phrases, and your luggage.</strong> None of them are difficult, but each one can make or break your pleasant trip if overlooked. Here's a quick guide to figure out what you actually need — then dive into the detailed articles for each topic.
      </p>
    </div>

        <nav class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">📋 In This Guide</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-3">
        <li><a href="#phone-apps" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">📱 Your Phone: Do You Have the Right Apps?</a></li>
        <li><a href="#connection" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">📶 Your Connection: eSIM, SIM Card, or Roaming?</a></li>
        <li><a href="#vpn" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🔒 Your VPN: Accessing the Internet Freely in China</a></li>
        <li><a href="#language" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🗣️ Your Language Skills: How Much Chinese Do You Need?</a></li>
        <li><a href="#luggage" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🎒 Your Luggage: What's Different About Traveling in China?</a></li>
        <li><a href="#checklist" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">✅ The Ultimate Pre-Departure Checklist</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

            <h2 id="phone-apps" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">📱</span> Your Phone: Do You Have the Right Apps?
      </h2>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">Here's the thing about China: <strong>the apps you use every day at home probably won't work here.</strong> Google Maps shows wrong directions. WhatsApp doesn't send messages. Uber doesn't exist. And you can't pay with your foreign credit card at most places.</p>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">You'll need to download a new set of apps before you arrive — WeChat and Alipay for payments, Didi for rides, Amap for navigation, and a few others.</p>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-12">Not sure which ones you actually need? The full guide breaks it down by category and tells you what each app does.</p>

      <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12 not-prose">
        <p class="text-gray-700"><strong>📖 Full guide:</strong> <a href="/fr/life/essential-apps/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">10 Apps You Need Before Traveling to China</a></p>
      </div>

      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

            <h2 id="connection" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">📶</span> Your Connection: eSIM, SIM Card, or Roaming?
      </h2>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">You'll need internet access the moment you land — for maps, translation, ride-hailing, and messaging. The question is which option suits your phone and your trip length.</p>

      <p class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Three ways to get online in China:</p>

      <ul class="space-y-4 mb-12">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3 bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-4">
          <span class="text-blue-500 text-xl mt-0.5">📱</span>
          <div>
            <strong class="text-gray-900">eSIM</strong>
            <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">Buy online before you go, activate on landing, no physical card needed. Best if your phone supports it and you want zero hassle. This type of card usually only provides data traffic and allows the use of overseas applications such as WhatsApp and YouTube. However, it does not offer Chinese mobile phone numbers. If you plan to use Didi or order takeout and other services that require receiving calls, it is recommended that you purchase a physical SIM card.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3 bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-4">
          <span class="text-green-500 text-xl mt-0.5">🆔</span>
          <div>
            <strong class="text-gray-900">Tourist SIM</strong>
            <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">Buy at the airport counter after you land. Requires your passport. Gives you a Chinese phone number. However, due to domestic network restrictions, many foreign apps won't work — you'll want to set up a VPN <strong>before</strong> departure.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3 bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-4">
          <span class="text-purple-500 text-xl mt-0.5">🌍</span>
          <div>
            <strong class="text-gray-900">International roaming</strong>
            <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">Most expensive, but zero setup. Check with your carrier first.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12 not-prose">
        <p class="text-gray-700"><strong>📖 Full guide:</strong> <a href="/fr/life/sim-card-guide/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Best SIM Card & eSIM for Tourists in China</a></p>
      </div>

      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

            <h2 id="vpn" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">🔒</span> Your VPN: Accessing the Internet Freely in China
      </h2>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">Here's a reality check: <strong>Google, Instagram, WhatsApp, Facebook, YouTube — none of these work on China's domestic internet.</strong> If you rely on any of them for communication, work, or entertainment, you need a VPN set up before you arrive.</p>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-12">The keyword is <strong>before</strong> — VPN websites and apps are blocked inside China, so you can't download one after you land.</p>

      <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12 not-prose">
        <p class="text-gray-700"><strong>📖 Full guide:</strong> <a href="/fr/life/vpn-guide/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Best VPNs for Traveling in China</a></p>
      </div>

      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

            <h2 id="language" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">🗣️</span> Your Language Skills: How Much Chinese Do You Need?
      </h2>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">You can absolutely travel China without speaking Chinese. But you'll have a much better time — better service, better prices, better interactions — if you learn even a dozen phrases.</p>

      <p class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">The honest breakdown:</p>

      <ul class="space-y-4 mb-12">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 bg-orange-50 rounded-xl">
          <span class="text-orange-500 text-xl">😅</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Zero Chinese:</strong> You'll survive. English is common in hotels and tourist spots, but expect frustration at restaurants and local shops.
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 bg-green-50 rounded-xl">
          <span class="text-green-500 text-xl">👍</span>
          <div>
            <strong>10–15 phrases:</strong> You'll be fine. Being able to say "thank you," "how much," and "check please" changes how people treat you.
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 bg-blue-50 rounded-xl">
          <span class="text-blue-500 text-xl">🚀</span>
          <div>
            <strong>50+ phrases:</strong> You're ahead of most travelers and will navigate independently.
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12 not-prose">
        <p class="text-gray-700"><strong>📖 Full guide:</strong> <a href="/fr/life/chinese-phrases/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Essential Chinese Phrases for Travelers</a></p>
      </div>

      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

            <h2 id="luggage" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">🎒</span> Your Luggage: What's Different About Traveling in China?
      </h2>

      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">Packing for China isn't drastically different from any other trip — but there are a few things that catch first-timers off guard:</p>

      <ul class="space-y-3 mb-12">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <span class="text-red-500 text-xl">🚻</span>
          <span class="text-gray-700">Public toilets often don't have toilet paper (bring your own)</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <span class="text-red-500 text-xl">🗺️</span>
          <span class="text-gray-700">Google Maps won't work in China (download local maps)</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <span class="text-red-500 text-xl">🌡️</span>
          <span class="text-gray-700">The climate varies massively between north and south</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <span class="text-red-500 text-xl">👟</span>
          <span class="text-gray-700">You'll walk a lot more than you expect</span>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12 not-prose">
        <p class="text-gray-700"><strong>📖 Full guide:</strong> <a href="/fr/life/packing-guide/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">What to Pack for China — Seasons & Climate Guide</a></p>
      </div>

      <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />

            <h2 id="checklist" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-4xl">✅</span> The Ultimate Pre-Departure Checklist
      </h2>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-12 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse bg-white rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-gray-900 text-white">
              <th class="px-6 py-4 font-bold">Done?</th>
              <th class="px-6 py-4 font-bold">Task</th>
              <th class="px-6 py-4 font-bold">Helps with</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100"><td class="px-6 py-4">☐</td><td class="px-6 py-4">Download WeChat and Alipay, set up payment</td><td class="px-6 py-4">Paying for everything</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 bg-gray-50"><td class="px-6 py-4">☐</td><td class="px-6 py-4">Install Didi, Amap, Trip.com</td><td class="px-6 py-4">Getting around</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100"><td class="px-6 py-4">☐</td><td class="px-6 py-4">Buy an eSIM or check roaming plan</td><td class="px-6 py-4">Staying connected</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 bg-gray-50"><td class="px-6 py-4">☐</td><td class="px-6 py-4"><a href="/fr/life/vpn-guide/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Set up a VPN</a></td><td class="px-6 py-4">Accessing blocked sites</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100"><td class="px-6 py-4">☐</td><td class="px-6 py-4">Download Google Translate offline pack or Pleco</td><td class="px-6 py-4">Communicating</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 bg-gray-50"><td class="px-6 py-4">☐</td><td class="px-6 py-4">Learn 10 basic Chinese phrases</td><td class="px-6 py-4">Daily interactions</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100"><td class="px-6 py-4">☐</td><td class="px-6 py-4">Pack power bank, tissues, adapter</td><td class="px-6 py-4">Avoiding common problems</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 bg-gray-50"><td class="px-6 py-4">☐</td><td class="px-6 py-4">Save digital copies of passport + visa</td><td class="px-6 py-4">Emergency backup</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

        <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-8 not-prose">
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">📚 Related Guides</h3>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="/fr/life/essential-apps/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100">
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">📱 10 Apps You Need Before Traveling to China</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">The essential app toolkit for China travel</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/fr/life/sim-card-guide/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100">
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">📶 Best SIM Card & eSIM for Tourists</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Compare all your connectivity options</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/fr/life/vpn-guide/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100">
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">🔒 Best VPNs for Traveling in China</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Stay connected to the apps you need</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/fr/life/packing-guide/" class="block bg-white rounded-xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition border border-gray-100">
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">🎒 What to Pack for China</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Season-by-season packing advice</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  
    <!-- Sources -->
    <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Sources</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
        <li>Compilation guide — sources distributed across individual articles on this site.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>